{
  "id": "generic-feed",
  "name": "Generic Feed",
  "label": "Generic Feed",
  "schemaVersion": 5,
  "catalogVersion": 1,
  "installMode": "recipe-or-json",
  "icon": "≡",
  "category": "reading",
  "description": "A generic RSS feed, configured by your agent — paste the prompt, give it a feed URL, and it shows one entry at a time.",
  "bundle": {
    "entry": "index.html",
    "files": {
      "index.html": "<div class=\"gf\">\n<div id=\"gf-prompt\">\n<p>No feed data has been pushed to this app yet.</p>\n<h3>Set up the feed</h3>\n<p>Copy this prompt into a Kody-connected agent:</p>\n<p class=\"gate-hint\"><code>Please set up a feed push for my kody-os app \"generic-feed\". Fetch the RSS feed at the URL below, then using Kody execute against kody:@hypercubed/kody-os, read the app's current state and set the full feed with the fetched items using the act action \"set_feed\". Do not overwrite the feed if the fetch fails, the fetched XML cannot be parsed, or the current feed cannot be read or parsed. The feed is RSS XML with one item per entry, each with title, link, pubDate, and a plain-text description, newest first, at most 14 entries.<br><br>– RSS feed URL: [paste the RSS feed URL here]<br>– App id: generic-feed<br>– Action: set_feed<br>– Format: RSS XML, newest first, at most 14 entries</code></p>\n<p>The app will show the latest entry once a push lands, with Previous and Next to step through entries.</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"gf-viewer\" style=\"display:none\">\n<div class=\"feed-nav\">\n<button id=\"gf-prev\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Previous\" title=\"Previous\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polyline points=\"15 18 9 12 15 6\"></polyline></svg></button>\n<span id=\"gf-pos\"></span>\n<button id=\"gf-next\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Next\" title=\"Next\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polyline points=\"9 18 15 12 9 6\"></polyline></svg></button>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"gf-title\"></h2>\n<div id=\"gf-date\" class=\"feed-date\"></div>\n<div id=\"gf-body\"></div>\n<p id=\"gf-linkp\" style=\"display:none\"><a id=\"gf-link\" href=\"#\">Open source</a></p>\n</div>\n<p id=\"gf-note\" style=\"display:none\">Stored feed could not be read.</p>\n</div>\n<style>\n\n.feed-nav { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; align-items: center; margin: 12px 0 12px 0; }\n.feed-nav button { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n\n#gf-pos { font-size: 18px; text-align: center; white-space: pre-wrap; padding: 0 12px; }\n/* Empty page: no bundle font or sizing of its own, so it reads\n * like the Help app, which carries no bundle CSS and lets the\n * shell theme style its prose, headings, and code. */\n#gf-title { font-size: 20px; margin: 16px 0 4px 0; }\n.feed-date { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; }\n#gf-body { white-space: pre-wrap; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; }\n#gf-body p { margin: 0 0 12px 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n#gf-body a, #gf-link { color: #000; text-decoration: underline; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: break-all; }\n#gf-note { font-size: 18px; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/* Generic Feed viewer. Read-only: no act() calls, no fetch, no\n * copy control, no local storage. State is read from the JSON\n * seed the shell renders before this bundle (bridge path), with\n * the shell span readout as fallback. Pure functions are defined\n * first so Node tests can load this script without a DOM and call\n * them directly; DOM wiring is guarded by typeof document. */\nfunction gfEscape(text) {\n  return String(text).replace(/&/g, \"&amp;\").replace(/</g, \"&lt;\").replace(/>/g, \"&gt;\").replace(/\"/g, \"&quot;\").replace(/'/g, \"&#39;\");\n}\nfunction gfUnescape(text) {\n  return String(text).replace(/&lt;/g, \"<\").replace(/&gt;/g, \">\").replace(/&quot;/g, '\"').replace(/&apos;/g, \"'\").replace(/&#39;/g, \"'\").replace(/&#x27;/g, \"'\").replace(/&amp;/g, \"&\");\n}\nfunction gfStripPunct(url) {\n  var punct = \"\";\n  while (url.length > 0) {\n    var last = url.charAt(url.length - 1);\n    if (last === \".\" || last === \",\" || last === \";\" || last === \":\" || last === \"!\" || last === \"?\" || last === \")\" || last === \"]\") {\n      punct = last + punct;\n      url = url.slice(0, -1);\n    } else {\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n  return [url, punct];\n}\nfunction gfLinkify(escapedText) {\n  var re = /(https?:\\/\\/[^\\s<]+)/g;\n  return escapedText.replace(re, function (match, bareUrl) {\n    var parts = gfStripPunct(bareUrl);\n    var clean = parts[0];\n    var punct = parts[1];\n    return '<a href=\"' + clean + '\">' + clean + '</a>' + punct;\n  });\n}\nfunction gfTagValue(block, tag) {\n  var re = new RegExp(\"<\" + tag + \"[^>]*>([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)</\" + tag + \">\");\n  var m = re.exec(block);\n  if (!m) { return \"\"; }\n  var v = m[1];\n  if (v.indexOf(\"<![CDATA[\") === 0) { v = v.slice(9); }\n  if (v.slice(-3) === \"]]>\") { v = v.slice(0, -3); }\n  return gfUnescape(v);\n}\nfunction gfParseFeedRegex(text) {\n  var items = [];\n  var re = /<item>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/item>/g;\n  var m;\n  while ((m = re.exec(text)) !== null) {\n    var block = m[1];\n    items.push({\n      title: gfTagValue(block, \"title\"),\n      link: gfTagValue(block, \"link\"),\n      guid: gfTagValue(block, \"guid\"),\n      pubDate: gfTagValue(block, \"pubDate\"),\n      description: gfTagValue(block, \"description\") || gfTagValue(block, \"content:encoded\")\n    });\n  }\n  return items;\n}\nfunction gfFormatPubDate(raw) {\n  if (!raw) { return \"\"; }\n  var d = new Date(raw);\n  if (isNaN(d.getTime())) { return \"\"; }\n  return d.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { weekday: \"long\", year: \"numeric\", month: \"long\", day: \"numeric\" });\n}\nfunction gfIsWellFormedFeed(text) {\n  if (text.indexOf(\"<rss\") !== -1) { return true; }\n  if (text.indexOf(\"<channel\") !== -1) { return true; }\n  if (text.indexOf(\"<feed\") !== -1) { return true; }\n  return false;\n}\nfunction gfParseFeed(text, domParser) {\n  var feed = String(text || \"\");\n  if (feed.trim() === \"\") { return { items: [], status: \"empty\" }; }\n  var items = [];\n  var parsedByDom = false;\n  if (domParser) {\n    try {\n      var doc = domParser.parseFromString(feed, \"text/xml\");\n      var errors = doc.getElementsByTagName(\"parsererror\");\n      if (!errors || errors.length === 0) {\n        var els = doc.getElementsByTagName(\"item\");\n        var i, el;\n        for (i = 0; i < els.length; i++) {\n          el = els[i];\n          items.push({\n            title: gfDomChild(el, \"title\"),\n            link: gfDomChild(el, \"link\"),\n            guid: gfDomChild(el, \"guid\"),\n            pubDate: gfDomChild(el, \"pubDate\"),\n            description: gfDomChild(el, \"description\") || gfDomChild(el, \"content:encoded\")\n          });\n        }\n        parsedByDom = true;\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      parsedByDom = false;\n    }\n  }\n  if (!parsedByDom) {\n    items = gfParseFeedRegex(feed);\n    if (items.length === 0 && !gfIsWellFormedFeed(feed)) {\n      return { items: [], status: \"unparseable\" };\n    }\n  }\n  items.reverse();\n  return { items: items, status: \"ok\" };\n}\nfunction gfDomChild(parent, tag) {\n  var i, node;\n  for (i = 0; i < parent.childNodes.length; i++) {\n    node = parent.childNodes[i];\n    if (node.nodeType === 1 && node.nodeName === tag) {\n      return node.textContent || \"\";\n    }\n  }\n  return \"\";\n}\nif (typeof document !== \"undefined\" && document.getElementById) {\n  (function () {\n    var viewer = document.getElementById(\"gf-viewer\");\n    var promptEl = document.getElementById(\"gf-prompt\");\n    var noteEl = document.getElementById(\"gf-note\");\n    var prevBtn = document.getElementById(\"gf-prev\");\n    var nextBtn = document.getElementById(\"gf-next\");\n    var posEl = document.getElementById(\"gf-pos\");\n    var titleEl = document.getElementById(\"gf-title\");\n    var dateEl = document.getElementById(\"gf-date\");\n    var bodyEl = document.getElementById(\"gf-body\");\n    var linkP = document.getElementById(\"gf-linkp\");\n    var linkA = document.getElementById(\"gf-link\");\n    var items = [];\n    var index = 0;\n    function readFeed() {\n      var feed = \"\";\n      try {\n        if (typeof window !== \"undefined\" && window.KodyBridge) {\n          var scriptEl = null;\n          try { scriptEl = document.currentScript; } catch (err) { scriptEl = null; }\n          var section = null;\n          var el = scriptEl;\n          while (el) {\n            if (el.getAttribute && el.getAttribute(\"data-app-id\")) { section = el; break; }\n            el = el.parentNode;\n          }\n          if (!section) {\n            var sections = document.querySelectorAll(\"section[data-app-id]\");\n            if (sections.length > 0) { section = sections[0]; }\n          }\n          if (section) {\n            var store = window.KodyBridge.create(section, { fieldTypes: { feed: \"string\" } });\n            var val = store.get(\"feed\");\n            if (typeof val === \"string\") { feed = val; }\n          }\n        }\n      } catch (err) {\n        feed = \"\";\n      }\n      if (!feed) {\n        var seeds = document.querySelectorAll('script[data-kody-state-seed=\"1\"]');\n        var s, parsed;\n        for (s = 0; s < seeds.length; s++) {\n          try {\n            parsed = JSON.parse(seeds[s].textContent);\n            if (parsed && typeof parsed.feed === \"string\") { feed = parsed.feed; break; }\n          } catch (err) { }\n        }\n      }\n      if (!feed) {\n        var p = document.querySelector('p[data-field=\"feed\"]');\n        if (p) {\n          var span = p.querySelector(\"span\");\n          if (span) { feed = span.textContent || \"\"; }\n        }\n      }\n      return feed;\n    }\n    function render() {\n      if (items.length === 0) { return; }\n      var item = items[index];\n      var title = item.title || (\"Entry \" + (index + 1));\n      titleEl.textContent = title;\n      var dateText = gfFormatPubDate(item.pubDate);\n      dateEl.textContent = dateText;\n      var desc = item.description || \"\";\n      var paragraphs = desc.split(/\\n\\s*\\n/);\n      var html = \"\";\n      var i;\n      for (i = 0; i < paragraphs.length; i++) {\n        if (paragraphs[i].trim() === \"\") { continue; }\n        html += \"<p>\" + gfLinkify(gfEscape(paragraphs[i])) + \"</p>\";\n      }\n      if (html === \"\") { html = \"<p></p>\"; }\n      bodyEl.innerHTML = html;\n      if (item.link && (item.link.indexOf(\"http://\") === 0 || item.link.indexOf(\"https://\") === 0)) {\n        linkA.setAttribute(\"href\", item.link);\n        linkP.style.display = \"\";\n      } else {\n        linkP.style.display = \"none\";\n      }\n      posEl.textContent = (dateText || title) + \"\\n\" + (index + 1) + \" of \" + items.length;\n      prevBtn.disabled = index <= 0;\n      nextBtn.disabled = index >= items.length - 1;\n    }\n    function init() {\n      var feed = readFeed();\n      var result = gfParseFeed(feed, (typeof DOMParser !== \"undefined\") ? new DOMParser() : null);\n      if (result.status === \"empty\" || result.items.length === 0) {\n        viewer.style.display = \"none\";\n        promptEl.style.display = \"\";\n        if (result.status === \"unparseable\") {\n          noteEl.style.display = \"\";\n        } else {\n          noteEl.style.display = \"none\";\n        }\n        return;\n      }\n      items = result.items;\n      index = items.length - 1;\n      promptEl.style.display = \"none\";\n      noteEl.style.display = \"none\";\n      viewer.style.display = \"\";\n      render();\n      prevBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n        if (index > 0) { index = index - 1; render(); }\n      });\n      nextBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n        if (index < items.length - 1) { index = index + 1; render(); }\n      });\n    }\n    if (document.readyState === \"complete\" || document.readyState === \"interactive\") {\n      init();\n    } else {\n      document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", init);\n    }\n  })();\n}\n</script>\n"
    }
  },
  "ui": {
    "title": "Generic Feed",
    "hideState": true,
    "placements": [
      "page"
    ]
  },
  "stateSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "initial": {
      "feed": ""
    },
    "fields": {
      "feed": {
        "type": "string",
        "maxLength": 250000
      }
    }
  },
  "actions": {
    "set_feed": {
      "description": "Set the full RSS feed XML, newest first, at most 14 entries.",
      "args": {
        "value": {
          "type": "string",
          "required": true,
          "maxLength": 250000
        }
      },
      "effects": [
        {
          "op": "set",
          "field": "feed",
          "fromArg": "value"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
